  "modelName": "Co-ops of Whatcom County",
  "modelNote": "Every co-op we could verify in Whatcom County, coloured by kind, with the documented ties between them. Lines are only ties with a public source — every line's popup says what the tie is and where it came from. Absence of a line means no tie was found, not that none exists. Two Skagit organisations (NABC and Puget Sound Food Hub, Mount Vernon) are included because they built Whatcom-serving co-ops; zoom out to see them. Not mapped: Bellingham housing co-ops (a Bellingham Housing Co-op Resource Center exists, but the names that surfaced online — Pacific Heights, Eight Oaks and others — appear to be British Columbia co-ops, and no Bellingham address could be confirmed); the Nooksack Tool Co-op (forming 2016–19, status and location unknown); Organic Valley member dairies (no local site). Main source: Cascade Cooperatives' Whatcom & Skagit co-op map. Researched Sep 2026 by Marc Pierson with Claude Opus 5.5. — From the RCN Map issue \"whatcom-wa--cooperatives\", sent to the Graph Tool 2026-09-28. Positions follow the map, nudged apart where points overlapped. Each node's _onMap link opens it on the map. Contacts (website, phone, email, address, people) added as node properties from the RCN Map issue file, checked Sep 2026.",
